# The trial of pod-rootfs in podvm (T-058), at podvm main 20ea781
# (pod-rootfs.commit), after pod-extract.patch (pod-rootfs.needs): podvm
# applies pod-extract.patch first, then this patch, and each applies clean
# in that order. pod-extract.patch carries the take of T-139 (payload_head
# and stage_file), which podvm's code needs with the pod-enter of v0.11.0.
# The patch was made at podvm 2616bd7 and made again on 20ea781 after
# pod-extract.patch: the tag lines of crates/podvm-image keep the pod-oci
# lines, and docs/runtime-state.md has one pod-* row for each crate, each
# at 0.11.0, with pod-extract, pod-oci and pod-rootfs, and no flate2 row.
# crates/podvm-complete keeps podvm's glue over the crate: Options (the
# flags), names() (each name that podvm writes into a root, with the values
# of earlier releases: 99podvm, the CA marker, podvm-host-ca-,
# .podvm-mknod-, the comment of pacman.conf), entry(id) (the T-04xx entry
# of each fixup id), Fixup and Step with their entry, Report with banner(),
# degradations() and json() (the same text and fields), settings(rootfs,
# opts) (podvm_probe::settings() for $PODVM_STORE in the space message, the
# host bundle of podvm_image::tls, the originals in <rootfs>/../.complete-orig),
# and reach::probe, the bounded HEAD over podvm_image::net that answers the
# probe of the crate. 13 files leave podvm, and podvm-extract leaves the
# dependencies of podvm-complete. The gate's pin of the write test goes (the
# test moves), and the citations of the moved files name pod-rootfs. Each
# podcrates tag moves to v0.11.0.
# podvm's tests of the touched crate and the integration tests that start a
# payload (each start runs the completion); clippy of the workspace and
# rustfmt of the touched crates, as podvm's gate.yml runs them; the
# runtime-state rows; podvm's record gate; each Rust toolchain of the
# workflows against the rust-version of podcrates; and the binary `podvm`
# for x86_64 musl, with podcrates' static check.
cargo test -q -p podvm-complete
cargo test -q -p podvm --bin podvm
cargo test -q -p podvm --test store_gates
cargo test -q -p podvm --test detached_stdio
cargo test -q -p podvm --test curated_refusals
cargo clippy -q --workspace --all-targets -- -D warnings
cargo fmt -p podvm-complete -p podvm -p podvm-gate --check
cargo build -q -p podvm --bin podvm
# podvm's gate finds the root of the repository from the path of its binary,
# so it runs from target/release/, with document-state beside it (gate.yml).
cargo build -q --release -p podvm-gate && cargo build -q --release -p podvm-release --bin document-state
mkdir -p target/release && cp "${CARGO_TARGET_DIR:-target}/x86_64-unknown-linux-musl/release/podvm-gate" "${CARGO_TARGET_DIR:-target}/x86_64-unknown-linux-musl/release/document-state" target/release/
# docs/runtime-state.md lists each direct git or registry dependency with its
# locked version. The patch gives the rows of the git form (pod-core,
# pod-enter, pod-guest, pod-hostprobe, pod-proxy, pod-rootfs, pod-supervise,
# pod-term and pod-tls at 0.11.0); the trial's path form has no row for
# them. Each other row of the patch must be the generated one.
grep -v '^| .pod-' docs/runtime-state.md > target/runtime-state.patch.md && python3 scripts/document-state.py --write && grep -v '^| .pod-' docs/runtime-state.md | diff target/runtime-state.patch.md -
./target/release/podvm-gate
python3 -I "$PODCRATES/scripts/check-consumer-toolchains.py"
sh "$PODCRATES/scripts/check-static.sh" "${CARGO_TARGET_DIR:-target}/x86_64-unknown-linux-musl/debug/podvm"
